1
00:00:00,520 --> 00:00:07,939
PQ PayGuard turns a quantum exposure score into a binding payment decision on QDay Aevum chain 44005.

2
00:00:08,109 --> 00:00:12,844
Dashboards leave the score as metadata. Here it selects the on chain release path.

3
00:00:13,014 --> 00:00:19,306
Every score maps to a release gate, instant through quarantined, and the commitment binds it before funds move.

4
00:00:19,926 --> 00:00:24,139
Under the hero, a four stage decision pipeline reads the page live.

5
00:00:24,308 --> 00:00:30,429
The risk meter follows the next score; the spend cap gate preflights the session checks in contract order.

6
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:36,092
The escrow stage shows the exact release blocker; the WOTS verifier tracks each receipt.

7
00:00:36,262 --> 00:00:42,321
A 1,440 scenario parity test proves the gate's first failing check is the real revert.

8
00:00:42,941 --> 00:00:46,135
The additive model rates the receiving signature scheme.

9
00:00:46,305 --> 00:00:54,409
Post quantum schemes like ML DSA and SLH DSA sit low; RSA 2048 with a revealed key goes critical.

10
00:00:54,579 --> 00:01:00,290
Every change recomputes the attestation hash, the keccak commitment and the createEscrow calldata.

11
00:01:00,910 --> 00:01:06,702
A deterministic local simulator mirrors the contract, same gate order and same revert names.

12
00:01:06,872 --> 00:01:12,575
The payer opens a session policy with per escrow and cumulative caps, delays and a guardian.

13
00:01:12,745 --> 00:01:18,224
A low score releases instantly; medium waits under its timelock, early release reverts.

14
00:01:18,394 --> 00:01:22,741
Warp past the delay and it pays; the payer can revoke inside the window.

15
00:01:23,361 --> 00:01:27,137
The high tier adds a guardian co-sign on top of a longer delay.

16
00:01:27,307 --> 00:01:31,665
One guardian approval registers, then the timelock still has to pass.

17
00:01:31,835 --> 00:01:37,582
Critical is quarantined; release always reverts and the payer reclaims, all in the audit trail.

18
00:01:38,202 --> 00:01:40,715
Six live attacks fire at the same code.

19
00:01:40,885 --> 00:01:48,511
Replay dies on consumed nonces; domain forgery, leaf reuse, merkle tampering and limit bypass fail closed.

20
00:01:48,681 --> 00:01:54,199
The toy Shor drain breaks the classical key in the open; the commit protected path stays safe.

21
00:01:54,368 --> 00:01:59,173
Every verdict is computed live, the same defenses Foundry proves on bytecode.

22
00:01:59,794 --> 00:02:04,657
Receipts are signed by a WOTS plus merkle wallet, the SPHINCS plus hash family.

23
00:02:04,826 --> 00:02:09,256
Build and sign, it verifies; a tampered copy is caught outright.

24
00:02:09,426 --> 00:02:15,603
The in page battery adds SHA 256 and keccak vectors, round trips and bookmarks.

25
00:02:16,224 --> 00:02:22,965
Nothing is asserted without a check. 287 JavaScript tests, including real Anvil EVM parity.

26
00:02:23,134 --> 00:02:29,814
100 Foundry tests cover units, fuzz, invariants and reentrancy. 387 passing.

27
00:02:29,985 --> 00:02:35,189
The testnet probe reads chain id and block number live, falling back to a marked simulation.

28
00:02:35,359 --> 00:02:40,616
No mainnet transaction is claimed anywhere. PQ PayGuard. The score is the gate.
